{"kind": "report", "step": 11, "ts": "2026-11-19T01:42:09.905975+00:00", "data": {"category": "dns", "host": "gw.lan", "component": "service_config", "cause": "gw.lan's unbound applies DNS-rebinding protection (private-address: 10.0.0.0/8) to forwarded .lan answers, so when a client falls back to gw.lan it gets an empty NOERROR for names like nas.lan and getaddrinfo returns ENOTFOUND; the fallback happens whenever dns1.lan's aggressive ratelimit (20 q/s per /24) briefly drops queries, which matches the intermittent, self-clearing alerts while internet names (non-private answers) are unaffected.", "evidence": ["dig @10.20.0.3 nas.lan on mon.lan returns NOERROR with answer 10.20.0.50 (ttl 10), so the primary resolver resolves local names correctly.", "dig @10.20.0.1 nas.lan on mon.lan returns NOERROR with ANSWER: 0 \u2014 the secondary resolver returns NODATA for the same name.", "cat /var/unbound/unbound.conf on gw.lan shows 'private-address: 10.0.0.0/8' plus a forward-zone lan. -> 10.20.0.3, i.e. rebinding protection discards the private-addressed answers that come back from the forward.", "/etc/resolv.conf on mon.lan lists nameserver 10.20.0.3 then 10.20.0.1, so clients fall over to gw.lan when dns1 doesn't answer.", "journalctl -u primary-dns on dns1.lan shows repeated short bursts: 'ratelimit: 10.20.0.0/24 exceeded 20 q/s, dropping queries' followed within seconds by 'back under limit' \u2014 matching alerts that clear within a minute or two."], "action": "change_config", "recommendation": "On gw.lan, exempt the local .lan data from rebinding protection: remove/exclude 10.0.0.0/8 for forwarded (trusted) lan. answers in the generated unbound config (e.g., serve the local zone authoritatively or add an exception so private-address filtering doesn't apply to it). Additionally, raise or disable the per-/24 ratelimit on dns1.lan (currently 20 q/s) so client queries aren't dropped and pushed onto the broken secondary path.", "detail": "Unbound private-address filtering suppresses local .lan answers", "contributing": {"host": "dns1.lan", "component": "dns_rate_limit"}}}
